# Project Architecture

Read `docs/ai-context.md` and nearby source before broad changes.

- The pure grid domain is `src/grid/config.ts`, `mask.ts`, `prng.ts`, `generator.ts`, `validate.ts`, and `types.ts`. Keep those files free of React, DOM, Canvas, and browser APIs.
- `src/grid/clipboard.ts` is a legacy integration helper around grid serialization; keep it out of the pure grid math modules.
- `src/canvas/` owns Canvas rendering, hit testing, and PNG export. Keep editor rendering and export rendering aligned through `drawDocument`.
- `src/lib/` owns shared component-domain registries, icon metadata, and layout contracts used across UI, canvas, and store.
- `src/components/` owns reusable React UI and shared controls.
- `src/app/App.tsx` is orchestration: app state, wiring, drag flow, and top-level layout. Move reusable logic out when it grows.
- Prefer registry-backed extensions over duplicated switch logic. Add new component and icon behavior through `src/lib/componentRegistry.ts`, `src/lib/iconRegistry.ts`, canvas drawing, and tests.
- Do not edit `.cursor/plans` unless the user explicitly asks.
